Z||000028||BRIAN CORNELIUS||05-31-2000||10:12 AM||||I converted my speedometer to a 200 MPH face on an '84 Fiero by using a 7.3728 MHz crystal. After looking around I found a local supplier who can supply them and the capacitor if an engine swap is completed to make your tach read right. They are: Chris Electronics Distributors in Roseville, Mn. There telephone number is 1-800-356-6599 and there web site is <A HREF="http://www.chriselectronics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.chriselectronics.com</A> <BR>It would be very helpful is someone with  electrical knowlekge could post the crystal ratings that are need for various speedometer ratings, say, 100 to 200mph in 10 mph increments.<P>||||reg||10
