Z||000041||terryk||06-06-2000||02:05 PM||||I know this isn't the techno-geek section, but rather than trying to find a weird crystal, I took a 74LS628 VCO from National and built a simple circuit to replace the crystal. You can adjust it so the speedo reads correctly. <P>Anyone that has some basic electronics experience can whip out the circuit. One chip, about 10 R's and C's and a pot to adjust the output frequency. <P>If someone cares, I can find my schematic and send it to them. A bit more work, but it ends the search for the correct crystal for your custom 350MPH speedo. And yes, the odo and trip read correctly too.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 06-06-2000).]||||reg||1
